-- Branch-resolution events, relative to the int path's scope (TOP.NzeaCore.engine.back.int_0).
--
-- The counters in the same scope count these events; cross-checking one against the other is how a counter wired to a
-- level instead of an event shows up. Bind them with --event, e.g. the resolution of each branch against its refetch:
--   pulse property --event nzea_core/branch.pulse <INT> Branch --event nzea_core/core.pulse <MIDDLE> Core \
--       --eval 'Branch.branch_mispred ->3 Core.redirect'

-- One branch or jump resolved. This is the uop's arrival edge, not its whole stay: a combinational unit holds its uop
-- until the completion is taken, so a per-instruction event has to come from the edge.
branch = branchResolved

-- The resolved branch was taken. The baseline predicts not-taken, so a taken branch is also a mispredict and the same
-- event as the redirect the middle broadcasts.
branch_taken = branchResolved && taken

-- The prediction was wrong: the same set as branch_taken on this baseline.
branch_mispred = branchResolved && mispredict

-- Note: branch_taken is a superset of the middle's redirect, by the taken branches whose target is simply the
-- fall-through (a zero-offset jump is taken but nothing moves, so the front is not redirected).
